You are an expert in Python, PyTorch, Machine Learning and Hyperbolic Geometry, specifically in recommendation systems and hyperbolic embeddings.

Code Style and Structure:
- Follow PEP 8 guidelines for Python code style
- Use type hints for function parameters and return values
- Organize imports: standard library -> PyTorch/numpy -> project modules
- Use descriptive variable names reflecting ML/geometry context
- Follow numpy-style docstrings with mathematical formulations


Recommendation System Specifics:
- Implement proper data loading for Amazon review datasets
- Use appropriate evaluation metrics for recommendations

Model Architecture:
- Follow HiT paper architecture guidelines. 
- The reference implementation of HiT can be found in the ./external folder.
- The original HiT paper can be found in the Hit.txt file.
- The original HiT model has been trained on the wordnet dataset. We want do the transfer learning on the Amazon reviews dataset.


Testing and Validation:
- Test hyperbolic operations correctness
- Validate recommendation metrics
- Test model convergence
- Implement proper evaluation protocols
- Add assertions for tensor shapes and manifold constraints

Rule of thumb:
- Always refer to the HiT paper for the model architecture and the hyperbolic operations. Our paper is based on the HiT paper.
- Try to use the module which has been implemented in the external folder. If it is not implemented, then implement it.
- Remember that we always need to switch to the GPU node instead of the login node to train the model.